#usda 1.0
(
    doc = """Test fixture for the daylight app's agent tools (server/test): a 20 x 12 x 10 m block whose four facades and roof
are quad meshes (1 m quads, front side outwards), and a tall neighbouring slab 6 m in front of Facade_S. Z up, metres.
/Site is turned 30 degrees counter-clockwise, so with the app's north at 0 (true north = +Y) Facade_N faces NNW (330),
Facade_E ENE (60), Facade_S SSE (150) and Facade_W WSW (240): each still counts as the side it is named after. On 21
March (London) the neighbour keeps the sun off Facade_S for most of the day, while Facade_N gets the late afternoon sun:
Facade_S is the least sunny facade. Variant set option on /Site/Block: base, or overhang (a 2 m deep horizontal slab
along the top of Facade_S)."""
    defaultPrim = "Site"
    metersPerUnit = 1
    upAxis = "Z"
)

